      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Policy and corporate choices absolutely shape the *pace and nature* of the transition, even if the ultimate technological potential for AI is fixed. Strong regulation can direct AI development towards more beneficial, human-centric uses, forcing certain \"unnatural\" outcomes to be un- or down-prioritized. Therefore, the debate is less about *if* the change will happen, and more about *how we choose to steer the development and its societal impact right now",
      "source": "target",
